WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.293
Microsoft's new coding models landed in GitHub Copilot on 17 November.

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:11.942
The headline: 98% of GPT-6.1 Sol's performance, at 40% of the cost.

00:00:14.502 --> 00:00:15.490
Hi, I'm Quota.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.440
The per benchmark numbers sit inside the chart on Microsoft's model page.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.756
I pulled them out.

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:26.568
Three of the four benchmarks were run by Microsoft, on its own

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:28.688
platform, in the Copilot command line tool.

00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:33.078
That is also the harness the model was trained in with reinforcement learning.

00:00:33.478 --> 00:00:34.474
It matters.

00:00:34.474 --> 00:00:40.945
Opus scores 78.7 on Terminal-Bench there, and 87.64 in another harness and setup.

00:00:41.345 --> 00:00:45.647
Only FrontierCode came from outside, and Artificial Analysis does not list MAI

00:00:45.647 --> 00:00:47.081
Code 2 at all.

00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:51.150
Averaged, the numbers reproduce.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.192
63.2 against 64.1 and 65.3.

00:00:54.192 --> 00:00:57.842
Microsoft even rounded its ratios down.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.969
Think of cost per task as a rectangle.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:05.373
Its width is the price of a token, its height is how

00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:06.791
many tokens the agent burns.

00:01:07.211 --> 00:01:10.087
MAI Code 2's price is a quarter of Sol's.

00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:13.922
But on DeepSWE it burned about twice the tokens, so it costs

00:01:13.922 --> 00:01:15.201
half, not a quarter.

00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:17.748
That price is a launch promotion.

00:01:17.748 --> 00:01:22.713
On 17 May 2027 it doubles, and the two rectangles are the same size.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:26.565
Now divide by the pass rate, since failures are billed too.

00:01:26.565 --> 00:01:30.621
At list price, MAI Code 2 is the dearer one per resolved task.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.389
Flash is half of GPT-6 Luna's price for now, and 65% of

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:37.802
its cost per task.

00:01:38.222 --> 00:01:42.721
Then its price becomes Luna's, token for token, and it costs 130%

00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:44.221
of Luna per task.

00:01:44.221 --> 00:01:46.096
It still passes more tasks.

00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:50.436
The model card disagrees with itself.

00:01:50.436 --> 00:01:55.301
Its autonomy table puts MAI Code 2 at 60.2 on DeepSWE.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:59.665
The headline table says 73.2, and nothing explains the gap.

00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:04.822
On the hardest terminal benchmark, MAI Code 2 sits below Haiku.

00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:09.026
Microsoft says long horizon work is out of scope, and it shows.

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:11.986
It is in Copilot today.

00:02:11.986 --> 00:02:15.182
Flash is on every plan, and in Foundry as a preview.

00:02:15.562 --> 00:02:17.603
No weights, and no outside benchmark yet.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.953
The arithmetic is honest, on Microsoft's own harness.

00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:25.857
Half the discount is the price, and the price doubles in May.

00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:31.934
Microsoft's harness, price times tokens, and a promotion with an end date.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:32.984
Thanks for watching!

00:02:33.404 --> 00:02:35.505
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:35.505 --> 00:02:36.105
I'm Quota.

00:02:36.105 --> 00:02:36.405
Bye!
